abstract:
Given a general dyadic grid ${\mathscr{D}}$ and a sparse family of cubes ${\mathcal S}=\{Q_j^k\}\in {\mathscr{D}}$, define a dyadic positive operator ${\mathcal A}_{{\mathscr{D}},{\mathcal S}}$ by $${\mathcal A}_{{\mathscr{D}},{\mathcal S}}f(x)=\sum_{j,k}f_{Q_j^k}\chi_{Q_j^k}(x).$$ Given a Banach function space $X({\mathbb R}^n)$ and the maximal Calder'on-Zygmund operator $T_{
atural}$, we show that $$\|T_{
atural}f\|_X\le c(n,T)\sup_{{\mathscr{D}},{\mathcal S}}\|{\mathcal A}_{{\mathscr{D}},{\mathcal S}}f\|_{X}.$$ This result is applied to weighted inequalities. In particular, it implies: (i) the "two-weight conjecture" by D. Cruz-Uribe and C. P'erez in full generality; (ii) a simplification of the proof of the "$A_2$ conjecture"; (iii) an extension of certain mixed $A_p$-$A_r$ estimates to general Calder'on-Zygmund operators; (iv) an extension of sharp $A_1$ estimates (known for $T$) to the maximal Calder'on-Zygmund operator $T_{
atural}$.

We find the index of $\widetilde{
abla}$-quasi-conformally symmetric and $\widetilde{
abla}$-concircularly symmetric semi-Riemannian manifolds, where $\widetilde{
abla}$ is metric connection.
